WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 002, en. Timings are estimates from the script until the clip is rendered.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<v the roundhouse mother>Smoke's going straight up this morning. The thatch held through the night, then.

2
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:12.273
<v the Iron-Age elder>Held, aye. The wind off the estuary tried it. This hill takes everything the sea throws at it.

3
00:00:12.623 --> 00:00:19.546
<v the roundhouse mother>And gives it back. The children slept warm round the fire. That's all I asked of the night.

4
00:00:19.896 --> 00:00:27.588
<v the Iron-Age elder>Look there, down the slope to the north. Flat ground. Somebody will build on that one day, mark my words.

5
00:00:27.938 --> 00:00:36.785
<v the roundhouse mother>Build what? There's nothing up here but us, the cattle and the crows. No one has ever drawn a line round this hill.

6
00:00:37.135 --> 00:00:47.904
<v the Iron-Age elder>No line, no mark. We know where it ends by the walking of it. Ask anyone in the valley whose hill this is, they'll point at our smoke.

7
00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:56.331
<v the roundhouse mother>Then let them point. One house, one fire, one family. Anyone wants more of it can come and argue with me.

8
00:00:56.681 --> 00:01:03.604
<v the Iron-Age elder>They'd lose. Fetch the little ones. We'll walk the edge before the rain comes in over the water.

9
00:01:03.954 --> 00:01:10.108
<v Nia>Bore da. Yesterday we followed a name across the hill. Today, something older than any name.

10
00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:24.688
<v Nia>This is the Glamorgan-Gwent Archaeological Trust report. They dug south of St Dochdwy's church and found what they call a possible late Iron Age roundhouse, under a Roman villa of the second to fourth century. Published 1988.

11
00:01:25.038 --> 00:01:37.346
<v Nia>Mark the word 'possible'. The trench shows the outline of a round building beneath the villa. It doesn't show who lived in it, what they were called, or how long they stayed.

12
00:01:37.696 --> 00:01:48.850
<v Nia>And it doesn't tie anyone to the farm. No deed, no family line reaches back that far. The dig itself gets its own day, in 1988, where it belongs.

13
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:55.354
<v Nia>For now, just the ground. A round house, then stone laid over it. Tomorrow, the villa.
